stead of allowing them to detonate  later we would find out the steve was  not really dead but was just frozen in a  block of ice and after being found and  thought out he goes from super soldier  to superhero becoming one of the  founding members of the avengers and  saving the earth from an alien invasion  literally the story of captain america  is a scrawny kid gets rejected from the  military only to be experimented on by  the military and then he's frozen in ice  becomes a human popsicle gets thought  out and becomes a hero but still  steve was haunted by the trauma he  experienced as a soldier most of which  centered around  the loss of bucky in his second solo  film captain america the winter soldier  steve meets a guy named sam wilson while  jogging and it turns out sam is an air  force veteran who runs a support group  for veterans dealing with ptsd and it  turns out sam had also lost his best  friend in combat in afghanistan  so they had a lot in common and sam was  basically becoming steve's new bestie  now around this time captain america was  working with shield which was basically  a massive intelligence agency with  nearly unlimited resources that deals  with threats to the united states and  the planet but instead of using their  resources to engage in things like  humanitarian efforts  shield built weapons but as it also  turned out shield have been infiltrated  by hydra and they plan to kill a bunch  of people using shield weaponry so sam  decides he's going to help captain  america black widow and nick fury the  director of shield  stop hydra's plot and he also reveals  that during his time in the air force he  learned how to use a set of mechanical  wings to fly hence how he became known  as the falcon because the apparatus they  used to fly was called  the falcon now as they attempt to thwart  hydra's plan captain america and company  encounter an adversary named the winter  soldier who nearly kills  all of them and who also happens to be  none 